 (slider `0..100`), **default 20**. Analytic mode ignores it.
 
+**Superseded on the scene-referred path (2026-08-28/29).** There is no clamped HDR value left to
+compensate for, so a linear "boost" over a five-decade quantity is the wrong control.
+`Streak Amount` is read as **gain in stops, ten units per stop, 50 = physical 1.0**
+(`decisions/s7-glare-gain.md`): 0 = off, 100 = +5 stops, 150 = +10. The shipped default stays 50,
+which is now both physical and visible on a night practical — see the corrected note above. Off
+the switch the stored value keeps its original linear meaning exactly.
